Files and their relationship to upstream
----------------------------------------
models.py   models.py, REDUCED to the configuration of the released checkpoint
            (ViT-S, input 384, patch 16, head Linear(384, 1)). Edits, each
            marked "# TruePixels:":
            - PyTorchModelHubMixin removed (weights are loaded by
              app/m2_analysis/detectors.py from a SHA-256-checked safetensors
              file with load_state_dict(strict=True), never from_pretrained);
            - timm.create_model(..., pretrained=True) -> pretrained=False:
              upstream starts TRAINING from ImageNet weights; for inference
              every tensor is overwritten by the checkpoint, so nothing is
              downloaded;
            - the other size/patch branches and freeze_backbone (a training
              option) removed; an unsupported configuration raises.
            The forward pass is unchanged.

Preprocessing is the authors' test transform from dataloader.py
(get_transform(mode="test")): Resize(440) -> CenterCrop(384) -> [0, 1] ->
Normalize(ImageNet mean/std). It is implemented in detectors.py with
torchvision; the values are transcribed exactly.

Label convention: upstream's default label map is "real:0,fake:1" and eval
applies a sigmoid to the single logit, so sigmoid(logit) = P(fake). Verified
by reproducing the authors' eval_using_huggingface.ipynb outputs on their
five DALL-E 2 test images (0.9988, 0.9878, 0.9569, 0.9516, 0.7860) to four
decimals on CPU and CUDA - tests/test_commfor.py.

Numerics (not a vendored edit): on CUDA, PyTorch runs convolutions in TF32 by
default, which moved the last sample to 0.7655. detectors.py therefore computes
the patch-embedding projection (Conv2d, kernel = stride = 16) as unfold +
matmul - the same linear map with the same tensors - so the full-precision
result is reproduced on every device without changing process-wide flags.
